{
  "$comment": "175 real custom-research prompts, as used as AI/enrichment columns in spreadsheet-style GTM tools, classified by hand against the RichAPI catalog. The prompt texts and titles are third-party content and are not vendored; only the classification is. It exists so the coverage claim in SKILL.md is a measurement rather than an impression, and so a reviewer can disagree with a specific row instead of with a vibe. tests/skills/research-agent/question-corpus.test.mjs re-derives every count from `prompts`.",
  "source": "175 custom-research column prompts from real GTM workflows (not vendored)",
  "source_prompt_count": 175,
  "classified_by": "by hand, one row at a time",
  "tiers": {
    "routed": "a named endpoint's own output IS the answer; the plan prices it exactly",
    "grounded": "the route is deterministic but returns a DOCUMENT; a reader has to find the answer in it, and may not",
    "local": "no fetch at all — reasoning or formatting over columns the row already carries. Zero credits",
    "unreachable": "no endpoint and no public document carries it; the answer is an explicit null"
  },
